  "slug": "protein-model-93eb",
  "summary": "New preprints pair protein language model embeddings with dynamics, structure, reaction or geometric inputs to predict variant effects, kcat, PTMs and more.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the specialization of protein sequence representations for defined prediction tasks through added task-relevant information, rather than reliance on generic embeddings. DynamicsPLM adds molecular dynamics heads to a 35M-parameter model to predict zero-shot variant effects. HieraPTM combines sequence, language model and 3D structure features to move from PTM site recognition to functional phosphosite prediction. EnzRef models reactants and products separately against a frozen model, using reference-centered adaptation for kcat. SMSTPred and PhageLysClass apply embeddings to methyltransferase substrate specificity and phage lytic protein classes. CarmnaDD predicts nitrogenase activity from sequence with dual descriptors (R2 0.60, AUC 0.94). A methodological counterpoint: one benchmark finds that embedding anisotropy degrades remote-homology retrieval relative to MMseqs2 and Foldseek, and that ZCA whitening addresses it. Other items, including FoldMapper, MANTA, AbPoolRank and MicroDUET, address inverse folding, disordered ensembles, antibody–antigen complex ranking and genomic surveillance.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
